LibRaw 0.22.2: run xtrans_interpolate()'s tile loop serially even in the
OpenMP build. The 512-pixel tiles overlap by 16 and each tile reads pixels a
neighbouring tile may already have written back into image[], so the parallel
loop's output depends on thread scheduling (LibRaw issue #845). Upstream's fix
(7a9777a, corrected by 4e20414) writes to a temporary image instead; it is not
taken here. Fuji X-Trans decodes stay single-threaded in this step only, and
come out exactly as the serial build's.

Spektralab-X patch.

--- a/src/demosaic/xtrans_demosaic.cpp
+++ b/src/demosaic/xtrans_demosaic.cpp
@@ -174,9 +174,10 @@
   size_t buffer_size = LIBRAW_AHD_TILE * LIBRAW_AHD_TILE * (ndir * 11 + 6);
   char** buffers = malloc_omp_buffers(buffer_count, buffer_size);
 
-#if defined(LIBRAW_USE_OPENMP)
-# pragma omp parallel for schedule(dynamic) default(none) firstprivate(buffers, allhex, passes, sgrow, sgcol, ndir) shared(dir) 
-#endif
+  // Serial on purpose: the tiles overlap, and a tile reads pixels a
+  // neighbouring tile may already have written back, so the parallel loop's
+  // output depends on scheduling (LibRaw issue #845). Serial output is what
+  // the single-threaded build always produced.
     for (int top = 3; top < height - 19; top += LIBRAW_AHD_TILE - 16)
     {
 #if defined(LIBRAW_USE_OPENMP)
